{"authored" [{"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93affbcfc570d3e78bf0e6370f5b131872b99610fc8a780f7efb9c65707e789e" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93affbcfc570d3e78bf0e6370f5b131872b99610fc8a780f7efb9c65707e789e" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "122de489a2fb17360002e9d6afdd30f518ad7c477b5db46c5a5d447bad6fc548" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/refer