ile_sha256" "93affbcfc570d3e78bf0e6370f5b131872b99610fc8a780f7efb9c65707e789e" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93affbcfc570d3e78bf0e6370f5b131872b99610fc8a780f7efb9c65707e789e" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/state.json" "file_sha256" "93affbcfc570d3e78bf0e6370f5b131872b99610fc8a780f7efb9c65707e789e" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "98c14270d651673c6323e15f9fd74a3d7f3a6ea82687614a1f267ae09c6b4976" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "98c14270d651673c6323e15f9fd74a3d7f3a6ea82687614a1f267ae09c6b4976" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "7ec96bbfa821ed234cba2197a000c1dc36384d64a7e6874afd69609553b58d5d" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "7ec96bbfa821ed234cba2197a000c1dc36384d64a7e6874afd69609553b58d5d" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "bafb75a05557c0b197170bf084226d09dd0c49e6611067b60d07ffcb6775fefa" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "bafb75a05557c0b197170bf084226d09dd0c49e6611067b60d07ffcb6775fefa" "basis" 1261 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037297/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-50411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡t⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2{sec}^{2}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=2{(\\sqrt{2})}^{2}=4.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 1=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50411" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-50411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\sqrt{2}⟨2,\\,1⟩"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}⟨4,\\,\\frac{1}{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50411" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨4+3{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(1)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(1)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=4+3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(1)=6\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=4{t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=12{t}^{2}+6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(1)=12\\cdot {1}^{2}+6\\cdot 1=18.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(1),\\,{y}^{′}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6,\\,18⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-349470" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨{e}^{3t}-4,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩,$ what is ${r}^{′}(t)?$\n\n${r}^{′}(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)={e}^{3t}-4,$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=6\\sqrt{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{2\\sqrt{t}}=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{e}^{3t},\\,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3e^{3t}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-347619" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{t}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),\\,8{e}^{t}⟩,$ ${r}^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}-1),$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=8{e}^{t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=8{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨{x}^{′}(t),\\,{y}^{′}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,{e}^{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-50373" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{2t}{{t}^{2}-1},\\,8{e}^{t}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-350217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\sqrt{1-t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ what is $|{r}^{′}(-1)|?$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|{r}^{′}(-1)|=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-350217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t)=\\sqrt{1-t},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-t}},\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(-1)=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-(-1)}}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t)=3{t}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(t)=6t,\n$$\n\nand therefore,\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(-1)=6(-1)=-6.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(-1) & =⟨{x}^{′}(-1),\\,{y}^{′}(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}},\\,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, computing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{r}^{′}(-1)| & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}})}^{2}+{(-6)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{8}+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}} \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-350217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-350217" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-350217" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{\\frac{289}{8}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-5\\,j+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the derivative of $f(t)$  by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-0\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k \\\\  & =({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "({e}^{t}+\\operatorname{sec}⁡t)\\,i+(2{t}^{2}+t)\\,j"] ["math" "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k"] ["math" "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i-2\\,j+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k"] ["math" "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,j+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,k"] ["math" "{sec}^{2}⁡t\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130398" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "({e}^{t}+{sec}^{2}⁡t)\\,i+(2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+t)\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{{t}^{4}} \\\\ {t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{5}{{t}^{4}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]\\end{align