uestion" "q-130400" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{20}{{t}^{5}} \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{t}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1),\\,{t}^{3}⟩$ with respect to $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,t+1,\\,{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,2t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130390" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1},\\,(t+2)^{2}⟩$ at $t=\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t+2)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t,\\,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}},\\,2(t+2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute ${f}^{′}(\\pi )$ we substitute $t=\\pi $ into the expression for ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\pi ) & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2\\pi ⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩"] ["math" "⟨2\\pi ,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi -2)⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\pi ,\\,\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1},\\,2(2\\pi +1)⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130408" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{\\sqrt{{\\pi }^{2}+1}},\\,2(\\pi +2)⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${f}^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3}+5{t}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find ${f}^{′}(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}+5{t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({6}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ \\operatorname{sec}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {csc}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}+5t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32415" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{2}+10t \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {6}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡6\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the second derivative of  $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,{s}^{4}+10s,\\,55⟩$ with respect to $s.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}({s}^{4}+10s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(55)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,\\,4{s}^{3}+10,\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the second derivative by differentiating ${f}^{′}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4{s}^{3}+10),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,12{s}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},1⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s,4{s}^{3}+10,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-32416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,12{s}^{2},0⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the second derivative of $f(t)=t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{t}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}t)\\,k \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+({t}^{2}-t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,k \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k \\\\  & =-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(t+1)\\,k"] ["math" "(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k"] ["math" "(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k"] ["math" "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k"] ["math" "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i-(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(t+1)\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-77683" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+(2t-1)\\,k"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the second derivative of $f(t)=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+(2{t}^{3}+t-2)\\,k$ with respect to $t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the derivative of $f(t)$ by differentiating each component.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+t-2)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}\\,i-(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{t}\\,i+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThen, we calculate ${f}^{″}(t)$ by differentiating ${f}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{t})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{2}+1)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+6t\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+2t+1\\,k"] ["math" "2{t}^{2}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+t\\,k"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{t}\\,i-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t})\\,j+2t\\,k"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-130426" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-{e}^{t})\\,j+12t\\,k"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t) \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t){sec}^{2}⁡(2t) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{3}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{3}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{3}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡t+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(t)-{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123184" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2t)({tan}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sec}^{2}⁡(2t)),\\,-\\frac{3}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2})⟩,$ ${r}^{″}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\operatorname{csc}⁡t \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t{cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{3}⁡t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({t}^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{2}{t} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "85225cf1155529aedd557b37a5436acaa8d0c7f5cb94daeb967f8f6554b330d2"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t(\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+\\operatorname{csc}⁡t),\\,\\frac{2}{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "q-123171" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{csc}⁡t({cot}^{2}⁡t+{csc}^{2}⁡t),\\,-\\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/state.json" "file_sha256" "fd9259e7aac128c06df2398f8fd4b0a2453a823435f39c5cd3baede8ecdb26c6"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 10t^4 ,\\, 6\\ln t\\rangle,$ what is $\\mathbf r'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "855eebdbd1dda37df727ec7246e485d62f89e4e90fa3aa05ae872f8e0686a95c"} {"question" "e-609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We differentiate each component separately.\n\n- For the $x$-component $x(t) = 10t^4,$ we have\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 40t^3,\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\nx'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = 40\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)^3 = 5.\n$$\n\n- For the $y$-component $y(t) = 6 \\ln t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t)=\\frac{6}{t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n$$\ny'\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right) = \\dfrac{6}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)}=12.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}) & =⟨{x}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2}),\\,{y}^{′}(\\frac{1}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,\\,12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-609.json" "file_sha256" "855eebdbd1dda37df727ec7246e485d62f89e4e90fa3aa05ae872f8e0686a95c"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of  $\\mathbf f(t) = \\langle \\sin t ,\\cos t , t \\rangle$ at $t= \\dfrac{\\pi}4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "f5dae4d8ee9edbd403734b58315ed12a804fb4bae4d4e991cb3132a8ff8717a8"} {"question" "e-2398" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find $\\mathbf f'(t)$ by differentiating each component:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute $\\mathbf f'\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}4\\right),$ we substitute $t=\\dfrac{\\pi}4$ into the expression for $\\mathbf f'(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-2398.json" "file_sha256" "f5dae4d8ee9edbd403734b58315ed12a804fb4bae4d4e991cb3132a8ff8717a8"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle t^6,\\, t^5\\rangle,$ Calculate $\\mathbf r''(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "22d171b8be61036e25a9c08e5e0ee48a8b71a35555285a99216b9dedd6d5c996"} {"question" "e-611" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the second derivative of a vector-valued function, we find the second derivatives of the components.\n\n- For $x(t) = t^6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =6{t}^{5} \\\\ {x}^{″}(t) & =30{t}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) = t^5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =5{t}^{4} \\\\ {y}^{″}(t) & =20{t}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨{x}^{″}(t),\\,{y}^{″}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨30{t}^{4},\\,20{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =10⟨3{t}^{4},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14047818/example-611.json" "file_sha256" "22d171b8be61036e25a9c08e5e0ee48a8b71a35555285a99216b9dedd6d5c996"}] "usage" {"e-2398" [] "e-609" [] "q-50373" [] "q-32415" [] "e-611" []} "basis" 1702 "retractions" [[17592186198870 :question/problem "Calculate $f^{′}(t)$ given that $f(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}t^{3} + 5t^{2} \\\\ \\tan t \\\\ 6^{t}\\end{bmatrix}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186197456 17592186197457 17592186197458 17592186197459 17592186197460 17592186296339 17592186296340 17592186296341 17592186296342 17592186296343] "immutable_fields" [[17592186197455 :answer-field/correct] [17592186197455 :answer-field/id] [17592186197455 :answer-field/key] [17592186197455 :answer-field/type] [17592186296338 :answer-field/correct] [17592186296338 :answer-field/id] [17592186296338 :answer-field/key] [17592186296338 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
